An anonymous struct naming a type parameter is substituted with the parameter:
Go and Kotlin copy each generic function and struct per instantiation, and each
copy's `struct { v T }` is the package's one `struct { v int }`, declared once
beside the literal's. JavaScript keeps the generic function and reads a
property. A literal inlined out of `held` into another literal is typed by its
values, and the struct holding it is the one `{o={v=1}}` has, so assigning one
to the other compiles. A generic component spliced where it is written is
spliced at the types its call site bound, so its state and its method hold the
package's `struct { v int }` too.

deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `(?m)^\t[A-Z]\w*\s+(\*|\[\])?(any|T)$` -- every copy's struct field is concrete
deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `struct\{ [A-Z]\w* (\*|\[\])?(any|T)\b` -- no struct is spelled inline with T erased
deny out/kotlin/android/app/src/main/java/test/sngl/app/MainScreen.kt `\bAny\b` -- every copy's struct is concrete
deny out/kotlin/android/app/src/main/java/test/sngl/app/MainScreen.kt `: T\b` -- no struct field names a type parameter
deny out/none/html/index.html `unwrap__` -- JavaScript keeps the one generic function
deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `__anon_o_\w+_2` -- a struct holding a substituted one is the package's one declaration

